        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "a1f64781-d494-3a95-8065-1118389a2120",
                "word": "bilirubine",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "980e2e23-a20d-45b8-8290-83b2c585422f",
                        "entry_id": "a1f64781-d494-3a95-8065-1118389a2120",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "bilirubines"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9b410125-ccf2-33dc-a3bc-af56f42fb2d8",
                        "entry_id": "a1f64781-d494-3a95-8065-1118389a2120",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pigment biliaire jaune produit par la dégradation de la partie non-protéique de l'hémoglobine, i.e. de l'hème. C'est un tétrapyrrole linéaire de couleur jaune rougeâtre, de formule brute C₃₃H₃₆N₄O₆, produit et accumulé dans la bile du foie sous sa forme dite \\\"libre\\\" — à laquelle il donne sa couleur, qui est ensuite conjugué à l'acide glucuronique avant d'être excrété dans le plasma — forme dite \\\"conjuguée\\\" — puis éliminé au niveau du tractus intestinal et du rein."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "26b22afb-b5a8-4c54-84a3-7611e98a64f7",
                                "sense_id": "9b410125-ccf2-33dc-a3bc-af56f42fb2d8",
                                "text": "On détecte la bilirubine dans les liquides organiques grâce à la réaction de Gmelin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c54f4c81-917d-4f08-afd0-ec7090cd238c",
                                "sense_id": "9b410125-ccf2-33dc-a3bc-af56f42fb2d8",
                                "text": "La bilirubine conjuguée dans le sérum ou le plasma peut se présenter sous plusieurs variantes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e4d44b9e-1b6f-468a-bab0-4167523efe8b",
                        "source_entry_id": "a1f64781-d494-3a95-8065-1118389a2120",
                        "source_sense_id": "9b410125-ccf2-33dc-a3bc-af56f42fb2d8",
                        "target_lang_word": "bilirubin",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bilirubin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "633ffa98-d375-3d21-b4ff-cfdfd1cc40cf",
                                        "entry_id": "3c62d711-df66-3ce7-8894-2a233cb14959",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bile pigment that is a product of the breakdown of the heme portion of hemoglobin (which occurs within macrophages as they digest red blood cells), and which is responsible for the yellowish color seen in bruises. Extremely high levels of bilirubin may cause jaundice."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22e05798-5abd-4f35-8f7b-23074340937a",
                                                "sense_id": "633ffa98-d375-3d21-b4ff-cfdfd1cc40cf",
                                                "text": "The doctors said this was very common, just her new-born liver catching up with the rest of her — the build-up of bilirubin in her blood. The substance red blood cells produce when broken down."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3f659e43-9f2a-46dd-bde5-4ce02f30fb53",
                        "source_entry_id": "a1f64781-d494-3a95-8065-1118389a2120",
                        "source_sense_id": "9b410125-ccf2-33dc-a3bc-af56f42fb2d8",
                        "target_lang_word": "bilirubina",
